body:
## Roadmap binding
- Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING / RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR
- Level-2: R8D lineage-contamination precommit gate
- Exact base: PR #912 @ `109ec7fdfc0851a680aba2ffc5ceef51769dd290`

## Why this successor exists
PR #914 proved a useful zero-effect lineage-contamination gate, but it was built on the parallel #909 lineage. This PR selectively reconstructs only that gate on the stronger stable-source Phase36 line (#898 -> #912), preserving #912's source-stability witness, replayed R7 evidence, durable certificate-ledger binding, one-attempt ATTEMPTED fence, 64-KiB evidence budget and readback-only ambiguity reconciliation.

## New gate
- derives target ancestry and descendants from the existing verified skill library's `parent_skill_digest`; no second lineage graph;
- exact closure coverage is mandatory;
- missing parent, UNKNOWN or CONTAMINATED lineage blocks PREPARED;
- each lineage node requires three pairwise-distinct critics: provenance/structural, security/behavioral, semantic-consistency;
- all reviewers must be separate from the planned effect executor;
- review binds exact source, verified library, current governance, target consumer snapshot and effect executor;
- verified clean review + digest is persisted inside the existing Phase36 exposure attempt and reverified on restart;
- new policy path is frozen from candidate/tournament/promotion mutation;
- existing 64-KiB attempt envelope still applies after adding the review.

## Authority / effects
Review is evidence-only and cannot release a hold, activate a skill, mutate the library, execute Browser actions, schedule work, promote, install or self-update. It does not add a scheduler, evaluator, library, lifecycle or effect journal.

No live exposure effect is performed. Current GitHub/DB/runtime source-identity drift remains a hard blocker for any real effect. Exact-head CI is required before this slice can be considered qualified.

Stacked RSI memory-rehabilitation hysteresis slice on top of PR #910.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-memory-reliability-tier-v1-gpt @ 50b442fadb5ac88b41754395030b1f9e29728341

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-memory-rehabilitation-margin-v1-gpt @ aabff455c911fe96c42b4e227d8ba5a8fdb0c61c

This closes a reliability loophole in the initial quarantine policy: a memory with severe harmful history could previously leave QUARANTINED as soon as later helpful evidence merely balanced the harmful evidence.

New contract:
- harmful history becomes sticky once exact harmful evidence reaches 2 receipts or discounted harmful evidence reaches the severe threshold;
- balancing or contradictory evidence is not enough to restore candidate guidance;
- quarantine exit requires at least 2 exact-context externally verified HELPFUL receipts and a strict weighted helpful margin of +1 over harmful evidence;
- cross-context helpful evidence alone cannot rehabilitate a quarantined memory;
- rehabilitated harmful history returns as COLD, never directly HOT;
- the original harmful evidence remains in the Experience Graph and remains queryable;
- Experience Context Planner exposes severe-harm and rehabilitation-evidence state on selected memories;
- candidate synthesis receives only externally rehabilitated guidance and the trust root explicitly forbids candidate self-rehabilitation.

This is deterministic evidence hysteresis over immutable case-local utility. It adds no memory deletion, scalar reward, model-weight update, Browser/release/self-update authority or physical effect executor.

## Scope

Phase36A adds a **zero-effect** transition proof for releasing exactly one admission-held skill from `DORMANT_CAP` to bounded `EXPLORATION_ACTIVE`. It does not remove a hold, mutate retrieval exposure, activate a skill, schedule work, actuate Browser, promote code, or self-update.

Stacked base:
- `work/browser-final-2026-convergence-rsi-repair-v1 @ 82e95118ffd2fbbbb6c3279f4a968e897cd50a9c`
- parent draft PR #839 remains exact-head CI non-terminal.

## Invariants

- consumes an already eligible external exposure review;
- binds exact source SHA, verified library, current governance and proposed next governance;
- requires exactly one hold removal and exactly one DORMANT_CAP -> EXPLORATION_ACTIVE transition;
- rejects direct full ACTIVE release;
- rejects any non-target entry drift, governance-policy drift, extra hold delta, source drift or cross-stage evidence aliasing;
- requires a separate external release owner distinct from all review principals;
- requires read-only shadow canary, coalition ablation and memory-poisoning scan evidence;
- proof remains zero-authority and zero-effect;
- one-attempt effect semantics are declared for the future effect-bearing lifecycle step, but no effect is authorized here;
- both the existing exposure-review policy and this proof policy are frozen in candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

## Research basis

Post-step research is tracked append-only in Supabase. Current evidence favors open search/proposal freedom behind deterministic external acceptors, paired no-skill controls, sealed evaluator roots, and benchmark-poisoning resistance.

## Gates

Draft only. No hold-release effect until the parent canonical repair exact-head workflow set is terminal green and the effect is implemented inside the existing durable lifecycle journal with no blind retry after ambiguity.

Stacked RSI retrieval-influence evidence slice on top of PR #899.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-bounded-memory-utility-v1-gpt @ a639b1525ca46d1c33818cbaca8fd6453ce763af

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-retrieval-influence-evidence-v1-gpt @ 2328b9673f056f489ae7ab7bd85b2c8a7948a0e1

This closes the next memory-credit loop without assigning one trajectory reward to every memory that happened to be retrieved.

Implemented:
- requires a persisted exact Experience Context Plan, persisted external six-class evaluation bundle and current verified Experience Graph;
- any AMBIGUOUS external evaluation blocks memory influence learning;
- memory influence can be attached only to cases actually selected in the exact context plan;
- allowed attribution methods are external LEAVE_ONE_OUT or PAIRED_ABLATION;
- each assessed memory requires distinct verified baseline-without-case and treatment-with-case evidence;
- utility is generated as the existing case-local Experience Graph utility receipt;
- selected but unassessed memories receive no utility at all;
- the candidate cannot rate its own memory, share trajectory reward across co-retrieved memories, mutate candidate score or create scalar reward;
- graph advance after assessment invalidates application and requires reassessment rather than replay;
- receipt sets, candidate IDs/SHAs, selected partitions and exact case lineage are independently reverified;
- runtime persists the influence admission before applying utility receipts to the Experience Graph and restart replay re-verifies exact bundle/context/graph lineage;
- policy root is fenced from candidate mutation in isolated-builder, tournament and promotion roots.

No second scheduler, no parameter update, no Browser/release/self-update authority, no physical effect executor and no blind retry.

## Roadmap binding
- Canonical Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING
- Level-2: RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R8_5_FRESH_SOURCE_IDENTITY_BINDING
- Exact base: PR #891 @ fb0014cbb007d91f265f32f0a77a1d703f839346
- Initial exact head: 9cbce4afc5b136e5fe13569540b753c29e5aafac

## Purpose
Strengthen the current Phase36 certificate-only lineage by requiring fresh, exact GitHub ↔ DB authority ↔ runtime source convergence at certificate time. This selectively ports the source-identity/freshness semantics from PR #892 without merging its parallel lineage and without implementing the exposure effect.

## Implemented
- exact three-way GitHub / DB authority / runtime SHA equality;
- typed independent readbacks and exact readback digests;
- fixed freshness policy: 60 s max age, 30 s cross-plane span, 5 s future skew;
- runtime process-incarnation binding;
- Phase36 certificate now requires a verified FRESH_SOURCE_IDENTITY_CONVERGED certificate;
- source identity certificate digest is bound into Phase36 evidence;
- source drift/staleness blocks the certificate even when shadow/ablation/canary evidence passes;
- source-identity and exposure-release policy files are frozen in isolated-candidate and promotion trust roots;
- runtime trust-root set includes exposure release + source convergence + source freshness;
- focused negative tests cover source drift, stale readback, candidate mutation of acceptor roots and zero authority.

## Safety
No hold removal, no skill activation, no Browser/task/scheduler/execution/promotion/self-update authority, no production mutation, no second evaluator/library/scheduler/effect journal, and no automatic retry after ambiguity.

## Qualification
Draft/source-only. Predecessor R2/R3/R6/R7/R8 and this exact head must be terminal-green before any one-attempt exposure effect or R9 active promotion is considered.

Stacked RSI bounded-memory utility slice on top of PR #893.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-correction-retrieval-bridge-v1-gpt @ 3d5e1592bf50bc72619bccfa26b31977c40295ec

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-bounded-memory-utility-v1-gpt @ a639b1525ca46d1c33818cbaca8fd6453ce763af

This slice addresses the memory-reward contamination problem in self-evolving retrieval systems.

Implemented:
- a fixed-dimensional bounded utility state derived only from the existing verified Experience Graph retrieval;
- exact and cross-context HELPUL/HARMFUL/NEUTRAL evidence remain separate coordinates;
- utility receipts stay case-local; no trajectory-level reward state and no joint credit update across co-retrieved memories;
- exact-context utility remains dominant; cross-context evidence remains a 0.25 advisory prior;
- memory state exposes correction-target, success/failure and utility-sparse coordinates without carrying raw trajectories;
- deterministic memory modes: EMPTY, HARMFUL_DOMINANT, EVIDENCE_SPARSE, CORRECTION_GUIDED, BALANCED;
- the mode controls context breadth before candidate synthesis: harmful-dominant retrieval is capped at 4 cases, evidence-sparse at 6, correction-guided/balanced at 8;
- the candidate cannot set utility, choose the case cap, mutate the bounded state or turn it into scalar/global reward;
- intrinsic verifier recomputes coordinate totals, weighted evidence, posterior, mode and cap even without the source graph;
- full verification can independently recompute the state from exact graph/query/retrieval;
- the new policy root is fenced from candidate mutation in isolated-builder, tournament and promotion roots.

No second scheduler, no model-weight update, no browser/release/self-update authority, and no physical effect executor is introduced.

## Roadmap binding
- Canonical Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING
- Level-2: RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R2_ZERO_AUTHORITY_CONVERGENCE
- Exact predecessor: PR #834 @ 17dab7c920956631a985c701f43b1f3a4ed8a655

## Purpose
Close the authority-schema drift identified by the RSI capsule/audit without adding a new authority plane.

## Implemented
- adds shared `metaengine.rsi.zero-authority.v1` contract;
- Browser/task authority are mandatory explicit false, not implicit by omission;
- execution/scheduler/production-mutation/promotion/self-update/authority-effect and automatic retry are also fail-closed;
- optional future signing/direct-tool authority fields, if present, must be false;
- meta-profile shadow selection and shadow-comparison binding now reuse the same validator;
- stale shadow-comparison fixture is repaired to carry explicit Browser/task zero-authority;
- dedicated falsification tests cover omission, retry escalation and optional authority escalation.

## Safety
No Browser/task/scheduler/execution/promotion/self-update authority is added. No DB mutation, library append, skill exposure, production effect or retry path is introduced. No second scheduler/evaluator/lifecycle/CAS/effect plane.

Draft until exact-head CI is terminal and post-step research/checkpoint readback is recorded.

Canonical Level-1 milestone: CROSS-CUTTING
Level-2 milestone: RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R8_PHASE36_BOUNDED_EXPOSURE_EFFECT

Exact base:
`work/browser-final-2026-convergence-rsi-r8-exposure-certificate-current-v1-gpt @ fb0014cbb007d91f265f32f0a77a1d703f839346` (PR #891)

This draft now contains two evidence-gated slices.

R8A — certificate hardening:
- mechanically replay-verifies the exact R7 dormant retrieval review against the Phase34B admission attempt, successor library and current governance;
- binds the R7 review digest plus upstream admission-attempt digest;
- enforces separation of Phase36 reviewers from all R7 reviewers and the original Phase34B effect executor.

R8B — bounded one-attempt effect on the existing lifecycle:
- reuses RsiRuntimeSkillLifecycle and the existing runtime evidence ledger; no second scheduler, lifecycle, evaluator, CAS plane or effect journal;
- persists PREPARED before any effect and ATTEMPTED with effect_attempt_count=1 before the exposure mutation;
- performs a second exact pre-effect readback after ATTEMPTED;
- drift becomes RECONCILIATION_ONLY with no effect and no blind retry;
- exact effect removes only the target admission exposure hold and permits only DORMANT_CAP -> EXPLORATION_ACTIVE;
- ambiguous outcomes are resolved by readback only: either CONFIRMED_EXPOSURE_RELEASED or CONFIRMED_NOT_RELEASED_NEW_ATTEMPT_REQUIRED;
- full activation, promotion, Browser/task/scheduler/self-update authority remain forbidden.

Tests include the successful R7 -> R8 path, PREPARED restart recovery, and ATTEMPTED/no-effect restart reconciliation without replay.

Current exact head is source/test evidence only. Do not merge/promote until this exact head and its stacked R7/R8 predecessors have terminal qualification evidence.

Canonical Level-1 milestone: CROSS-CUTTING
Level-2 milestone: RSI_R8_CERTIFICATE_LEDGER

Base:
`work/browser-final-2026-convergence-rsi-r8-exposure-certificate-current-v1-gpt @ fb0014cbb007d91f265f32f0a77a1d703f839346`

This stacked slice does not execute an exposure release. It adds a bounded append-only runtime evidence ledger for externally verified Phase36 exposure certificates and integrates it into RsiRuntimeService.

Invariants:
- full Phase36 certificate verification occurs before persistence;
- durable-before-visible, restart-safe, idempotent evidence recording;
- rejected certificates remain auditable;
- self-rehashed authority widening fails closed;
- the ledger has no hold-release, retrieval-exposure, skill-activation, Browser, scheduler, promotion, signing, tool, or self-update authority;
- no second scheduler or effect journal is introduced;
- future one-attempt release execution remains blocked behind terminal exact-head qualification of the predecessor stack.

Draft/evidence-only. No production/runtime promotion.

Stacked RSI governed correction-retrieval bridge slice on top of PR #752.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-post-deployment-correction-trace-v1-gpt @ e44a1567938017f3b6dcf32c76b5f70cbdcf1eae

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-correction-retrieval-bridge-v1-gpt @ 3d5e1592bf50bc72619bccfa26b31977c40295ec

This closes a real authority gap in experience retrieval.

Previously the runtime accepted raw bridge_case_ids from the caller even though policy said candidate_can_select... = false. A caller that knew a case id could therefore steer cross-context retrieval without a persisted external selection artifact.

This slice changes that contract:
- direct non-empty bridge_case_ids are rejected at the runtime boundary;
- correction bridges must be selected by an external selector and persisted first;
- selection is exact-bound to source SHA, current base context plan, current query, current Experience Graph snapshot and opportunity;
- only verified FAILURE cases that have an existing fixed_by edge to a verified SUCCESS case are eligible;
- maximum 4 bridge cases;
- the selected failure and correction target identities/digests are embedded and reverified;
- the bridge becomes invalid after graph/context drift and must be reselected externally;
- openLearningEpisodeFromOpportunity consumes only a persisted bridge_selection_digest;
- bridge selection is retrieval signal only, never portability, execution, promotion, release or self-update authority;
- candidate cannot select bridges or mutate the bridge policy;
- runtime restart replay verifies the bridge against the exact graph state and embedded base plan.

No second scheduler, no browser effect executor, no release/self-update action, no blind retry.

## Roadmap binding
- Canonical Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING
- Level-2: RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R5_SOURCE_IDENTITY_CONVERGENCE
- Exact predecessor: `PR #834 @ 17dab7c920956631a985c701f43b1f3a4ed8a655`
- Exact head: `587adc76af09c14c6527662d5efcb3fb0c4f6d52`

## Purpose
Rebuild the R5 exact GitHub ↔ DB authority ↔ runtime identity gate directly on the current canonical-repair source instead of leaving it on the divergent #839 repair lineage.

## Implemented
- exact three-way 40-hex SHA equality is the only converged state;
- ancestry, semantic and version-string equivalence are explicitly forbidden;
- independent GitHub/DB/runtime readback digests are required;
- freshness certificate requires typed origins, exact inherited digests and runtime process-incarnation binding;
- fixed external timing policy: 60s max readback age, 30s max cross-plane span, 5s future skew;
- stale/future/misaligned readbacks and stale runtime heartbeat fail closed;
- candidates cannot author identity evidence/certificates or configure freshness;
- both R5 trust roots are included in the existing RuntimeService trust-root set;
- output remains evidence for later external admission review only and carries zero Browser/task/scheduler/execution/promotion/self-update authority.

## Live-state note
The gate does not synchronize any authority plane. Known live identities are currently not assumed equal; a drift result is therefore valid and must block admission rather than trigger automatic rewrites or updates.

## Qualification
Draft/source-only. No DB authority mutation, runtime update, Browser effect, promotion or self-update. Exact-head CI and independent current readback remain required.

Canonical Level-1 milestone: CROSS-CUTTING
Level-2 milestone: RSI Phase36 reviewed zero-effect certificate

Exact base:
`work/browser-final-2026-convergence-rsi-r7-provenance-review-v1-sol @ c8ab96d83a63aa03a40d37317b99e92a1ffe0dfe` (current PR #883 head at reconstruction)

This supersedes #888, whose parent advanced during construction.

Implemented:
- exact current -> next governance preview for one held skill only;
- current target must be DORMANT_CAP under admission hold; predicted next state is EXPLORATION_ACTIVE only;
- certificate consumes the already verified zero-effect matched exposure review;
- confirmed Phase34B admission provenance is digest-bound through the review;
- certificate-stage identities are disjoint from review identities and the original admission effect executor;
- extra shadow contexts, no-skill ablation, coalition ablation and READ_ONLY_SHADOW canary remain required;
- certificate stays zero-authority and cannot release the hold, change retrieval exposure, schedule work, promote, or self-update;
- future release effect must be a separate one-attempt transition in the existing lifecycle with exact pre-effect readback and no blind retry.

Draft/noncanonical until exact-head CI is terminal green and parent #883 is qualified.

## Roadmap binding
- Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING / RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR
- Level-2: R7 provenance-bound dormant retrieval review
- Exact base: PR #879 head `a5586a517dd7df008dcde351cc5ad8a13d0472e1`
- Exact head at creation: `07f2825a222e819b282a863c1a47a833d7e1b56a`

## Purpose
Selectively reconstruct the strongest zero-effect R7 review semantics on the hardened Phase35 exposure-hold lineage without importing the divergent PR #869 lifecycle/runtime field line.

## Implemented
- confirmed admission exposure provenance readback exists only for one exact `CONFIRMED_APPLIED_STORAGE_ONLY` Phase34B attempt;
- trusted-migration holds deliberately have no confirmed admission provenance and cannot qualify by hold membership alone;
- provenance binds admission certificate, storage effect identity, effect executor identity, confirmed transition, admitted successor library, current library and current governance;
- new dormant retrieval review requires exact held `DORMANT_CAP`, exact current library/governance and exact confirmed admission provenance;
- matched numeric evidence is internally checked: skill/reference successes must equal repairs-regressions;
- hard vetoes cover matched regressions, hard-invariant failure, negative transfer, cost/latency, harness, benchmark, memory, grounding, contamination, from-scratch replay, coalition ablation and marginal contribution;
- eligibility is fenced by both global active cap and dedicated `EXPLORATION_ACTIVE` slot capacity;
- five external review roles are pairwise distinct and separated from the storage-effect executor;
- runtime obtains library/governance/provenance internally and appends the review only to the existing RSI runtime ledger;
- review is zero-effect: no hold release, retrieval exposure, activation, Browser/task/scheduler authority, promotion, self-update or blind retry.

## Research mapping
- SkillOpt: bounded persistent artifacts + strict held-out gate + rejected-change memory; no force-accept semantics imported.
- DGM: retain empirically validated archive lineage; admission provenance is a stepping-stone, not activation authority.
- GEPA: preserve multidimensional evidence and avoid collapsing exposure to one scalar.
- OEO: optimizer freedom remains inside externally fixed objective/budget/data/evaluation boundaries.

## Checkpoints
- `RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R7A_CONFIRMED_EXPOSURE_PROVENANCE_20260919_V1`
- R7B implementation/research checkpoint follows exact-head readback.

Draft/noncanonical. No production/runtime effect and no promotion until exact-head CI is terminal green.

## Roadmap binding
- Canonical Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING
- Level-2: RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R7_FRESH_DORMANT_RETRIEVAL_REVIEW
- Exact predecessor: `PR #884 @ 044a575868eeef33d9dc442dbcb7d6f65a761ddc`
- Exact head: `7ef380f8d0b693da72bb4f49fcdbc6ec17e3ddb7`

## Purpose
Add the consumer-local, zero-effect retrieval review required between storage admission and any future bounded exposure release, directly on the current R6 lineage.

## Implemented
- new zero-authority `rsi-dormant-skill-retrieval-review.mjs`;
- exact internally read back confirmed Phase34B storage admission required;
- exact admission exposure-hold provenance is required and bound to current library + governance;
- trusted-migration holds have no confirmed admission provenance and therefore cannot produce review eligibility;
- paired control/treatment on identical instances, harness and budget;
- evaluator/consumer/retrieval integrity, hidden holdout, contamination and from-scratch replay;
- task/safety/security/process/outcome/efficiency non-regression;
- strict post-append improvement, coalition ablation and marginal contribution;
- active-cap plus dedicated EXPLORATION_ACTIVE slot capacity fences;
- reviewer identities separated from the storage-effect executor;
- RuntimeService writes only review evidence to the existing runtime ledger;
- review cannot release a hold, expose/activate a skill, schedule work, execute Browser effects, promote or self-update.

## Important repair
The older donor checked a stale `admission_exposure_hold` field. This reconstruction binds the actual current R6 fields `admission_exposure_held` and `admission_exposure_hold_external_release_required`.

## Qualification
Draft/source-only. No production/live mutation. Predecessor R2/R3 and R6 plus this exact head must qualify before R8 is considered canonical.

## Roadmap binding
- Canonical Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING
- Level-2: RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR_R6_PHASE35_EXPOSURE_HOLD
- Exact predecessor: `work/browser-final-2026-convergence-rsi-post821-repair-v1 @ 17dab7c920956631a985c701f43b1f3a4ed8a655`
- Exact head: `044a575868eeef33d9dc442dbcb7d6f65a761ddc`

## Purpose
Rebuild the useful Phase35 storage-vs-exposure semantics directly on the current R1-R3 repair lineage instead of merging older divergent Phase35 branches.

## Implemented
- persisted admission exposure-hold set inside the existing RsiRuntimeSkillLifecycle;
- every non-bootstrap append must bind the exact newly appended skill digests to holds;
- held skills are forced to DORMANT_CAP/non-composable even with later positive lifecycle evidence;
- one-attempt Phase34B append and reconciliation expose held-skill readback;
- hold mutation is rollback-safe during reconciliation;
- RuntimeService ledger surfaces storage-only hold evidence;
- trusted migration cannot attach a hold to an unchanged skill;
- historical library lineage and post-ATTEMPTED pre-effect readback from the current repair lineage are preserved.

## Authority
No Browser/task/scheduler/execution/promotion/self-update authority. No second scheduler, evaluator, skill library, lifecycle, CAS plane or effect journal. No live skill append or production mutation.

## Qualification
Source-only stacked R6 implementation. It must not become canonical or merge before predecessor R2/R3 exact-head CI is terminal green and this head passes its own exact-head qualification.

## Roadmap binding

- Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING / RSI_CANONICAL_REPAIR
- Level-2: R7 Dormant Retrieval / Exposure Review
- Exact base: `work/browser-final-2026-convergence-rsi-repair-v1 @ 82e95118ffd2fbbbb6c3279f4a968e897cd50a9c`
- Exact head: `a48844209ed5f78796bf2462e7229436882976c5`

## Why

The current repair line already separates storage from retrieval exposure and adds a zero-effect matched review. But hold membership alone is not sufficient release provenance: trusted migration/backfill can create held dormant skills without the exact Phase34B one-attempt admission path.

This successor converges the strongest provenance seam from PR #876 with the current matched-review/runtime line instead of creating another review or release plane.

## Change

- existing Phase34B lifecycle emits a read-only admission-exposure provenance receipt only for exactly one `CONFIRMED_APPLIED_STORAGE_ONLY` attempt for the held skill;
- receipt binds attempt digest, certificate, effect identity, effect executor, idempotency key, confirmed transition, admitted successor library, current library and current governance;
- direct/migration holds have no confirmed admission provenance;
- existing `rsi-skill-exposure-release-review` now requires that exact provenance;
- exposure reviewers must be separated from the original admission effect executor;
- runtime obtains provenance from the existing lifecycle and journals the provenance/attempt identities with the review;
- review remains zero-effect: it cannot release the hold, change retrieval exposure, activate a skill, schedule work, operate Browser, promote, install or self-update.

## Research-facing invariant

The matched review remains a consumer-scoped differential test:
- same-instance/matched reference;
- positive matched gain;
- zero functional regressions;
- negative-transfer veto;
- cost/latency veto;
- harness, benchmark-provenance, memory-safety and source-grounding gates.

This PR only proves that such evidence is attached to the exact storage-admission lineage. Phase36 release remains a separate one-attempt external-governance effect.

## Authority

Browser=false; task=false; scheduler=false; execution=false; release=false; promotion=false; self-update=false; production mutation=false; automatic retry=false.

## Qualification

Draft only. No production/live mutation. Exact-head CI must be terminal green before convergence. If the moving repair base absorbs equivalent semantics first, close this PR as superseded rather than merge duplicate policy.

Successor hardening over PR #874.

The donor Phase36 certificate already had the right zero-authority evidence envelope, but its preview accepted an opaque next_governance_digest without recomputing that digest from a supplied next governance object. This slice closes that seam.

Changes:
- adds canonical create/verify exposure preview bound to exact current + next governance;
- proves the target is currently admission-held DORMANT_CAP and that only that hold is removed;
- requires the resulting target state to be EXPLORATION_ACTIVE, never ACTIVE;
- rejects unrelated hold drift, non-target state drift and target evidence drift;
- certificate now validates against the supplied exact next governance;
- trust root freezes exact-next-governance requirement;
- still certificate-only: no runtime hold release/effect, no Browser/task/execution/promotion/self-update authority, no retry/scheduler.

This preserves #874's ablation, poisoning, grounding, negative-transfer, read-only canary and reviewer-SOD requirements rather than duplicating them.

Successor to superseded #870, reconstructed from the current exact Phase35 base f5d2e54bddc2a1bc52ea72e84ce0aae957469199 after that base independently converged the core exposure-hold semantics.

This PR ports only non-duplicating deltas:
- require the hold set to exactly match newly appended digests on every post-bootstrap library update, so a trusted migration cannot silently add a hold to an unchanged skill;
- remove duplicate hold insertion in the one-attempt path;
- make reconciliation hold mutation copy-on-write and rollback-safe if governance verification fails;
- expose held-skill identity through execute/reconcile results and RuntimeService ledger/readback;
- forward exact hold digests through the explicit trusted-migration surface;
- add focused regressions for hold mutation without append and runtime/reconciliation readback.

No second lifecycle, scheduler, append journal, release authority, Browser authority, promotion authority, or self-update authority is added. Production/live Browser remains unchanged and eligible_for_promotion=false.

## Roadmap binding
- Level-1: CROSS-CUTTING / RSI canonical repair
- Level-2: Phase36 certificate-only slice
- Exact base: f5d2e54bddc2a1bc52ea72e84ce0aae957469199
- Exact head at creation: a236cec56dfb8324c90292b5ad14206c281c507a

## Scope
Adds only the external, zero-authority certificate that may later authorize one bounded exposure-release attempt. It does not remove any hold and has no release executor.

Eligibility requires:
- exact verified library + current governance + bounded next-governance preview;
- held DORMANT_CAP target -> EXPLORATION_ACTIVE only;
- >=3 all-pass shadow contexts and hard-invariant pass;
- no-skill and coalition ablations;
- negative-transfer clearance;
- memory-poisoning scan;
- source grounding;
- READ_ONLY_SHADOW canary;
- pairwise-distinct governance/shadow/security/canary reviewers.

The certificate carries no release token and grants no Browser/tool/execution/promotion/self-update authority.

